{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>A portion as a portion they shall eat.</b> As for what is written concerning the sons of Eli — ' annex me, please, to one of the priesthoods, to eat bread' — which implies that they did not receive a portion: that is because the verse made distribution contingent on service, as it is written 'and he shall serve his brothers in the name of HaShem' — whoever serves, receives a portion. And the seed of Eli had not reached the age of twenty, to be fit for service, for they were thirty years old, as it is written concerning the sons of Eli: 'every increase of your house shall die men,' meaning young men." "<b>Beside his sales.</b> If he sold the house he inherited from his fathers, they may not say to him: you shall not take a portion, since you have [your own means]. Another interpretation: <b>beside his sales among the fathers</b> — the language of acquaintance, like 'a man from his acquaintance' (איש מאת מכרו), meaning: if he has acquaintances and relatives among his fathers who give him their offerings to offer them, he is permitted to offer them even though he is not of that watch."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The comment 'they were thirty years old' appears to conflict with the subsequent proof-text about dying young; rendered literally as it stands, the logic is difficult."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:19.131582727Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}